Meeting description

During the Week 1 team meeting, Abiral, Aakash, Tasnim, and Sebastian discussed and 
finalized the concept and title for the group project.

The team agreed to develop a Phishing Awareness Game aimed at teenagers aged 14–16 
years. The purpose of the game is to educate young users about phishing attacks, 
online scams, suspicious links, and safe internet practices through interactive 
gameplay and engaging scenarios.

After brainstorming several ideas and reviewing the project objectives together,
the team collectively finalized the game title and confirmed the project direction
for development and GitHub documentation. The discussion also included initial ideas
for gameplay mechanics, educational goals, and target audience engagement strategies.
